PASS e4-1a: conventions at n = 2, 3 (exact): the modes a+-_p satisfy the CAR, a-_p is the transpose of a+_p, the first basis vector is the Fock vacuum (a-_p|0> = 0 for all p), N = 3n/2 + sigma(K_n) is diagonal with spectrum 0..3n and multiplicities binom(3n, m)
PASS e4-1b: paired rotations at n = 2, 3 (exact, all 15 resp. 36 basis elements of so(3n)): sigma(X) equals the one-body operator sum_pq R_pq a+_p a-_q, where R is the real antisymmetric matrix of X on z; hence [sigma(X), N] = 0, and sigma(X) maps the one-quantum state a+_q|0> to sum_p R_pq a+_p|0>
PASS e4-1c: copy rotations at n = 3 (exact): sigma(C^{kl}) commutes with N, with N^(k) + N^(l), with N^(m) for m not in {k,l}, and with each direction number N_i = sum_k N_(k,i); it does not commute with N^(k); it equals sum_i (a+_(l,i) a-_(k,i) - a+_(k,i) a-_(l,i)); the three lifts close on so(3) as on vectors ([C^12, C^13] = C^23)
PASS e4-1d: copy boosts at n = 3 (exact): sigma((E_lk - E_kl)(x)G) = -sum_i (a+_(k,i) a+_(l,i) + a-_(l,i) a-_(k,i)); its matrix elements join only sectors with N differing by +2 or -2, both occurring; it commutes with N^(k) - N^(l) and with N^(m), m not in {k,l}, so each created pair has one quantum in constituent k and one in l; a generic paired boost of so(9,C) (random integer S) also changes N by exactly +-2, both occurring
