PASS e4-1f: gauge reading at n = 3 (exact): the quarter turn U = e^{(pi/2) sigma(C^{12})} = (1/8) prod_a (1 + 2 t_a), t_a the six commuting terms of sigma(C^{12}), is orthogonal, commutes with N and with N^(3), and maps N^(1) to N^(2): U N^(1) U^T = N^(2); the conjugate of sum_k kappa_k N^(k) has the same spectrum and, for kappa_1 != kappa_2, differs from it
PASS e4-2a: n = 4, rates (1,2,3,5) (exact): the endomorphisms of V_4 commuting with G_4, the diagonal l_G and K(x)G are sum_k (a_k + b_k G) on copy k (dimension 8), and the eta_4-isometries among them are the 16 copy reflections diag(+-1,+-1,+-1,+-1)(x)1_6
PASS e4-2b: copy reflections on sign patterns, n = 3..6 (exact, exhaustive): the coboundary map Z_2^n -> Z_2^E (s -> s_k s_l) has rank n-1 over Z_2, so the cycle space of the complete graph has rank c = (n-1)(n-2)/2 = 1, 3, 6, 10; the 2^E sign patterns fall into exactly 2^c orbits, and the signs of the c triangles (1,k,l), 2 <= k < l <= n, are constant on orbits and separate them
PASS e4-2c: interior time reversal B -> -B, n = 3..6 (exact, exhaustive): it flips the sign of every triangle and multiplies the sign of a cycle of length L by (-1)^L; no sign pattern of the complete graph is reflection-equivalent to its negative (the complete graph on n >= 3 vertices is not bipartite)
